**Plan, not yet applied.**

`buildRows()` in [report.js](src/report.js) already gives full rows, `owner` and `slow` included. `toTable()` in [format.js](src/format.js) drops those two on purpose, for width.

```js
// cli.js
if (argv.includes('--json')) {
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(buildRows(), null, 2) + '\n');
  return 0;
}
process.stdout.write(toTable(buildRows()) + '\n');
```

No changes needed in `report.js` or `format.js`. Say the word and I'll wire it in.
